From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: a BO big enough for a texture turned linear

A u-interleaved texture overwritten whole again and again (a video) is
turned linear in panfrost_ptr_unmap, in the BO it had. The linear
layout can be bigger: its rows are aligned to 64 bytes, the tiles only
to 16 pixels. An R8 video plane 784x203 (the U and V planes of DOOM 3
BFG's main menu video, 1567x406) needs 168896 bytes linear against
163072 tiled, in a 163840-byte BO; only an assert (gone in release
builds) stood in the way. That copy and every later upload of a frame
wrote past the end of the BO's mapping: into whatever was mapped after
it (another BO: GPU faults, corrupted job descriptors) or into nothing
(a crash in memcpy at a page boundary, glTexSubImage2D going back to
the menu). Such a resource now gets a new BO of the linear size; with
no memory for one it stays tiled.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_resource.c
@@ -1881,16 +1881,47 @@
                panfrost_resource_setup(screen, prsrc, DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR,
                                        prsrc->image.layout.format);
 
-               /* converting the resource from tiled to linear and back
-                * shouldn't increase memory usage...
-                */
-               assert(prsrc->image.layout.data_size <= panfrost_bo_size(bo));
+               /* The linear layout can be bigger than the tiled one: its
+                * rows are aligned to 64 bytes, the tiles to 16 pixels (an
+                * R8 784x203 video plane: 168896 bytes against 163072, a
+                * 163840-byte BO). Then the resource gets a BO big enough,
+                * else this copy and every later upload write past the end
+                * of the old one, into whatever is mapped after it. */
+               struct panfrost_bo *newbo = NULL;
 
-               util_copy_rect(
-                  bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].offset,
-                  prsrc->base.format, prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].row_stride,
-                  0, 0, transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height, trans->map,
-                  transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+               if (prsrc->image.layout.data_size > panfrost_bo_size(bo)) {
+                  perf_debug(ctx, "Linear layout bigger than the tiled BO: "
+                                  "%u > %zu bytes, new BO",
+                             (unsigned)prsrc->image.layout.data_size,
+                             (size_t)panfrost_bo_size(bo));
+                  newbo = panfrost_bo_create(
+                     dev, prsrc->image.layout.data_size,
+                     bo->flags & ~PAN_BO_DELAY_MMAP, bo->label);
+                  if (newbo) {
+                     panfrost_bo_unreference(prsrc->bo);
+                     prsrc->bo = newbo;
+                     prsrc->image.data.base = newbo->ptr.gpu;
+                     bo = newbo;
+                     panfrost_dirty_state_all(ctx);
+                  } else {
+                     /* no memory for it: tiled for good */
+                     panfrost_resource_setup(
+                        screen, prsrc,
+                        DRM_FORMAT_MOD_ARM_16X16_BLOCK_U_INTERLEAVED,
+                        prsrc->image.layout.format);
+                  }
+               }
+
+               if (prsrc->image.layout.modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) {
+                  util_copy_rect(
+                     bo->ptr.cpu + prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].offset,
+                     prsrc->base.format,
+                     prsrc->image.layout.slices[0].row_stride, 0, 0,
+                     transfer->box.width, transfer->box.height, trans->map,
+                     transfer->stride, 0, 0);
+               } else {
+                  panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
+               }
             } else {
                panfrost_store_tiled_images(trans, prsrc);
             }
